  /* The arrival, once, the way Messages does it. Armed by the script, so without it the exchange simply
     reads. The typing bubble pops in at the tail (a spring with a little bounce), the dots breathe, then
     the bubble grows into the message (a clip that opens, critically damped, with the text fading in as
     it does), and the reply is sent: it springs up from below the thread, anchored at its own tail. Then,
     a beat later, it is delivered, as Messages shows it: the conversation is anchored at its bottom, so
     the label is added below the reply and the whole thread rises by the label's height while
     "Delivered" fades in. Until then the thread sits that much lower. Springs are sampled into linear()
     easings, so all of it is CSS, off the main thread; browsers without linear() get the site's ease-out. */
  .thread { --receipt-h: calc(max(0.75rem, 0.55em) * 1.7); } /* the label's line and its margin, in its own em */
  .bubble__dots { display: none; }
  .contact.is-armed .thread__stamp, .contact.is-armed .bubble--them, .contact.is-armed .thread__reply, .contact.is-armed .thread__receipt { opacity: 0; }
  .contact.is-armed .bubble__dots { position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; width: 3.6em; height: 2.14em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.24em; }
  .contact.is-armed .bubble__dots i { width: 0.42em; height: 0.42em; border-radius: 50%; background: #8e8e93; opacity: 0.35; }
  .contact.is-playing .thread__stamp { animation: contact-fade 300ms ease both; }
  .contact.is-playing .bubble--them { transform-origin: 0 100%; animation: contact-pop 640ms var(--ease-out) 150ms both; }
  .contact.is-playing .bubble__body { animation: contact-grow 550ms var(--ease-out) 1900ms both; }
